==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|huguenot||Huguenot; also, a personal name and surname|lang=fr}}, diminutive of {{term|Hugo|lang=fr}}, {{term|Hugon|lang=fr}}, {{term|Hugues|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|gmh|en}} {{term|Hūg|lang=gmh}}, {{term|Hūc||Hugh, a man's name|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|gmh|en}} {{term|huge||mind|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|en}} {{term|hugu||mind, thought|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*huguz}}, {{term/t|gem-pro|*hugiz||mind}}, of unknown origin. Cognate with {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|hyge||thought, mind, heart, disposition, intention, courage, pride|lang=ang}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|hyū'gə-nŏt'}}, {{IPA|/ˈhju.ɡə.nɒt/}}

